     "I think this is happening because there is a group (maturity==9) with only one observation. If you remove that row from the data set, it works fine.<div><br></div><div>ggplot should give a better error or warning in this case, so I filed an issue:</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/issues/676\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/issues/676&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374562837000&amp;usg=AOvVaw30HnQVRhzjyh0NqtmbjA70\">https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/issues/676</a></div><div><br></div><div>-Winston</div><div><br></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Sep 27, 2012 at 1:58 PM, Styrkur Nams <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stat.d...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><br> Dear all,<br><br> This script worked two months ago, but now it doesn&#39;t and the only difference is that I updated the ggplot2 package:<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>qplot(lngtclass,data=ldm,geom=&quot;density&quot;,colour=maturity,adjust=0.15) <br><br>where x= lngtclass, and maturity is the aesthetic to subset the data.<br>         <br><br>I have tried several other examples from <a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374562837000&amp;usg=AOvVaw23Oa4n9kR4yJHTbCiW8sN6\">docs.ggplot2.org</a> and I always get an error when I add the second aesthetic with geom_density or stat_density.  I get the following errors:<br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<br><span style=\"text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-variant:normal;text-align:auto;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:normal;border-collapse:separate;text-transform:none;font-size:medium;white-space:normal;font-family:Arial;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(101,123,131);font-family:Monospace;font-size:10px;line-height:11px;text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap\"><pre style=\"font-family:Monospace;font-size:7.4pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(133,153,0)\">p &lt;- ggplot(ldm, aes(lngtclass)) \r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(133,153,0);white-space:pre-wrap\"></span><span style=\"color:rgb(133,153,0)\">p + geom_density(aes(fill=factor(maturity)), size=2)</span></pre></span></span><span style=\"text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-variant:normal;text-align:auto;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:normal;border-collapse:separate;text-transform:none;font-size:medium;white-space:normal;font-family:Arial;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(101,123,131);font-family:Monospace;font-size:10px;line-height:11px;text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap\"><pre style=\"font-family:Monospace;font-size:7.4pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">\r\n\r\n<span>Error in rowSums(vapply(x, is.finite, logical(nrow(x)))) : \r\n  &#39;x&#39; must be an array of at least two dimensions\r\n</span><span>Error in if (nrow(layer_data) == 0) return() : argument is of length zero</span></pre></span></span><br>If I try to use the old script, I get<br><br><span style=\"text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-variant:normal;text-align:auto;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;line-height:normal;border-collapse:separate;text-transform:none;font-size:medium;white-space:normal;font-family:Arial;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(101,123,131);font-family:Monospace;font-size:10px;line-height:11px;text-align:-webkit-left;white-space:pre-wrap\"><pre style=\"font-family:Monospace;font-size:7.4pt!important;outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-top-style:none;border-right-style:none;border-bottom-style:none;border-left-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;line-height:1.2\">\r\n\r\n<span>Error in unit(tic_pos.c, &quot;mm&quot;) : &#39;x&#39; and &#39;units&#39; must have length &gt; 0<br><font style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Any ideas?</span></font><br>\r\n\r\n\r\n<br><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Thanks!</span></font><span><font color=\"#888888\"><br><br><br></font></span></span></pre></span></span><span><font color=\"#888888\"><br>\r\n<br><br>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374562837000&amp;usg=AOvVaw31a9iLAwfgvyO9m0y0mVvB\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nTo post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nTo unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nMore options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\